'''Potions''' are consumable items that have a variety of different effects and bonuses. Players are able to make most of them at various levels with the [[Herblore]] skill using [[herb]]s and other ingredients.

Most potions act as a [[temporary skill boost]], but some have other effects, like curing [[poison]] or providing [[dragonfire protection]]. A player must add a [[Herblore secondaries|secondary ingredient]] to the [[Unfinished potion (disambiguation)|unfinished potion]], finishing the potion completely. A newly finished vial of potion contains three (3) doses of the potion. Some higher-level potions require a vial of [[coconut milk]] or [[Vial of blood|blood]] to be used instead of water.

Wearing an [[amulet of chemistry]] gives a 5% chance of creating a four (4) dose potion instead. A charged [[alchemist's amulet]] increases this chance to 15%. [[Prescription goggles]] give players a 10% chance to not consume a secondary ingredients when mixing potions. These items can be useful for conserving resources on [[Ironman Mode|Ironman accounts]] or for potions with rare or expensive ingredients.

Similar to the delay after eating [[food]], drinking a ''non-barbarian'' potion will delay your next potion consumption by 3 [[ticks]] (1.8 seconds). Notably, food and potions '''do not''' share the same timer, meaning it is possible to eat a piece of food then drink a potion in the same tick. Note that drinking barbarian mixes use the same timer that eating food does.

==F2P potions==
[[Strength potion]]: obtainable by giving the [[Apothecary]] {{NoCoins|5}} coins, one [[limpwurt root]] and [[Red spiders' eggs]].

[[Energy potion]]: obtainable by giving the Apothecary one [[chocolate dust]] and two [[Limpwurt root|limpwurt roots]].

[[Antipoison]]: obtainable by giving the Apothecary {{NoCoins|5}} coins, one [[limpwurt root]] and [[Cadava berries]].

